# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GO_0003823> (antigen binding)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "GOC:jl") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "ISBN:0198506732") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "ISBN:0721662544") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GO_0003823> "Binding to an antigen, any substance which is capable of inducing a specific immune response and of reacting with the products of that response, the specific antibody or specifically sensitized T-lymphocytes, or both. Binding may counteract the biological activity of the antigen. Antigen binding by an MHC protein complex allows the antigen to be displayed to a T cell or NK cell.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GO_0003823> "antigen binding")
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GO_0003823> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GO_0005488>)

